    {
      "id": "pz-about-txt",
      "name": "text-basic",
      "parent": "pz-about-c",
      "children": [],
      "settings": {
        "text": "One studio. One person on the call.\n\nI founded Profuzion in 1999 at a single desk in Winkler — not to follow design trends, but to help owners who have to be understood the first time and trusted the second. Lawyers, agents, shop floors, and front desks: the work has always been about clarity, not volume.\n\nThe stack changes every few years. The promise doesn't: a brand and site you can hand to a new hire without a translation layer. When you hire the studio, you work with me from first call to launch — no account manager, no handoff to someone who wasn’t in the room for the brief.\n\n// what we believe\nMost websites for service businesses look like they were ordered from a catalogue. Same hero photo. Same testimonial slider. Same forgettable trust.\n\nWe build brands and sites that read the way you sound across the desk — calm, certain, unmistakeably yours. The kind a referral lands on and finishes the call.\n— Profuzion · since 1999"
      },
      "label": "Founder + manifesto"
    },
